<p>I want to write about several games I&rsquo;ve been trying out for the last month, and once again I get stuck. Writing is just not the right medium for games. First, there&rsquo;s too much to say about each game, and I feel like I have to rave about each one until my fingers fall off. Second, they are visual — they need to be <em>seen</em>.</p>
<p>The answer is the same as it&rsquo;s always been: videos. But videos take time. Writing a long post takes a couple of hours, which can spread over a day or two. Making a video takes days, and it can stretch over <em>weeks</em>. It just doesn&rsquo;t scale, not with the time I have.</p>
<p><a href="https://taonaw.com/2026/04/23/things-i-want-to-do.html">It&rsquo;s a dilemma I keep facing</a>. I want to talk about these games because I enjoy them and I spend hours gaming each week, but I&rsquo;m not sure I want to spend two weeks or so working on a single video.</p>
